{"text": "Petrakis & Yoon CPAs, LLP\nMEMO TO FILE - LOAN APPLICATION PACKAGE\nClient: Three Sisters Bakehouse LLC (client no. 30418) | Prepared by Graham Petrakis, CPA | September 14, 2026\nPurpose\nThe client is applying to Columbia Gorge Community Bank for an SBA 7(a) term loan of $285,000 to build out a second production kitchen. The bank's reference is application no. CGCB-7A-2026-0418. We compiled the financial package and helped the members complete SBA Form 1919 and SBA Form 413. This memo records what was submitted and the open points.\nBorrower\nThree Sisters is an Oregon limited liability company formed March 9, 2019, EIN 93-4471208, NAICS 311811. It operates a retail bakery at 212 Oak Street, Hood River, OR 97031, under a lease with Ostrowski Family Properties LP (landlord contact Bernard Ostrowski III, 541-555-0122). Rent is $4,150 a month through 2031. It files Form 1065.\nMembers and guarantors\nName\tOwnership\tSSN\tDate of birth\tID\nAroha Ngata-Williams\t40%\t048-36-1142\t14 Feb 1985\tOR DL 4471902\nMei-Ling Zhou\t30%\t186824355\t1988-07-30\tOR DL A882047\nFatima al-Sayed\t30%\tITIN 9XX-XX-4471 applied for SSN\t06/21/1990\tPassport N01447729\n\nAll three will guarantee personally. Ms. Ngata-Williams is a New Zealand citizen and a lawful permanent resident (USCIS no. A-088-204-417). Ms. al-Sayed's adjustment of status is pending; the bank has said this does not disqualify her as a guarantor of a minority interest but wants her work authorization card, which expires 01/31/2027. Mei-Ling disclosed a Chapter 7 discharge in 2014 on Form 1919, question 7; a letter of explanation is in the package.\nFinancial summary\n2025 gross receipts $1,184,300; net income before guaranteed payments $142,760.\nYear-to-date through August 31, 2026: receipts $861,900, up eleven percent.\nExisting debt: equipment note with Wy'east Federal Credit Union, loan no. 70-0044187-L2, balance $38,412.66, payment $1,022 monthly.\nProjected DSCR after the new loan is 1.41.\nPersonal financial statements: Aroha's net worth $212,000; Mei-Ling's $96,500; Fatima's under 20k, mostly her vehicle.\nCollateral offered\nFirst lien on all business assets, including the deck oven (serial RV-DO4-2291-0087) and the spiral mixer (serial SM80-114477).\n2022 refrigerated delivery van, VIN 1FTBW3XG5NKA40917, Oregon plate 817 MKT.\nSecond deed of trust on Aroha's home at 1640 Belmont Avenue, Hood River (tax lot 03N10E35CB 04400); estimated equity $150,000.\nBanking\nOperating account at CGCB: routing 057426080, account 20044718830. Payroll account at Wy'east: account 881-0047-2. Loan proceeds and payments will run through the operating account.\nOpen points\nThe bank's underwriter asked for Form 4506-C transcripts for each guarantor. Mei-Ling's 2024 return was filed late; expect a question.\nMr. Ostrowski has not yet signed the landlord consent. He told Fatima he wants a personal guarantee on the lease extension first.\nFee for this engagement: $3,200 fixed, invoice PY-11872 sent 9/14/26. Questions to gpetrakis@petrakisyoon.example or (541) 555-0148.", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "453 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Graham Petrakis", "Bernard Ostrowski III", "Aroha Ngata-Williams", "Mei-Ling Zhou", "Fatima al-Sayed", "Ms. Ngata-Williams", "Ms. al-Sayed", "Mei-Ling", "Aroha", "Fatima", "Mr. Ostrowski", "gpetrakis"], "companies": ["Petrakis & Yoon CPAs, LLP", "Columbia Gorge Community Bank", "Ostrowski Family Properties LP", "Three Sisters Bakehouse LLC", "Oregon", "93-4471208", "NAICS", "Wy'east Federal Credit Union", "CGCB", "Petrakis Yoon"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.900000000372529, "modelMs": 41459.29999999888, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl", "routing", "phone", "record", "vin", "account", "money", "dob", "age90", "date", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 25, "text": "Petrakis & Yoon CPAs, LLP",